#: app_gateway/views.py:293
msgid ""
"\n"
"    <h5>Certificate</h5>\n"
"    <p>Defines how the TLS certificate for this hostname is issued.</p>\n"
"    <ul>\n"
"        <li><strong>Trusted certificate (HTTP validation)</strong>: Issued "
"through ACME (e.g. Let's Encrypt) and validated over HTTP. The hostname must "
"point to this server and ports 80/443 must be reachable from the internet.</"
"li>\n"
"        <li><strong>Trusted certificate (DNS validation)</strong>: Issued "
"through ACME and validated with a DNS record created using the selected DNS "
"credential. The server does not need to be reachable from the internet. When "
"the credential uses a delegation domain, the hostname zone only needs a "
"CNAME record pointing to it, shown when the credential is selected.</li>\n"
"        <li><strong>Self-signed certificate</strong>: Issued by the internal "
"Caddy CA. Browsers will show a security warning.</li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p>When the fallback option is enabled and a trusted certificate cannot "
"be issued, a self-signed certificate is used until the next successful "
"attempt. Without the fallback, the connection fails until the certificate is "
"issued.</p>\n"
"    <p>Use <strong>Retry certificate</strong> in the host list to request a "
"new attempt right away, for example after fixing the DNS or firewall.</p>\n"
"    <p><strong>Important:</strong> the certificate is requested as soon as "
"the configuration is applied. With HTTP validation, the hostname must "
"already point to this server: failed attempts count towards the Let's "
"Encrypt limit (5 per hour per hostname). If the DNS is not ready yet, use "
"DNS validation.</p>\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"    <h5>Certificado</h5>\n"
"    <p>Define cómo se emite el certificado TLS de este hostname.</p>\n"
"    <ul>\n"
"        <li><strong>Certificado de confianza (validación HTTP)</strong>: "
"emitido mediante ACME (p. ej., Let's Encrypt) y validado por HTTP. El "
"hostname debe apuntar a este servidor y los puertos 80/443 deben ser "
"accesibles desde internet.</li>\n"
"        <li><strong>Certificado de confianza (validación DNS)</strong>: "
"emitido mediante ACME y validado con un registro DNS creado con la "
"credencial DNS seleccionada. No es necesario que el servidor sea accesible "
"desde internet. Cuando la credencial usa un dominio de delegación, la zona "
"del hostname solo necesita un registro CNAME que apunte a él, que se muestra "
"al seleccionar la credencial.</li>\n"
"        <li><strong>Certificado autofirmado</strong>: emitido por la CA "
"interna de Caddy. Los navegadores mostrarán una advertencia de seguridad.</"
"li>\n"
"    </ul>\n"
"    <p>Cuando la opción de respaldo está habilitada y no se puede emitir el "
"certificado de confianza, se utiliza un certificado autofirmado hasta el "
"próximo intento correcto. Sin el respaldo, la conexión falla hasta que se "
"emita el certificado.</p>\n"
"    <p>Use <strong>Reintentar certificado</strong> en la lista de hosts para "
"solicitar un nuevo intento de inmediato, por ejemplo después de corregir el "
"DNS o el firewall.</p>\n"
"    <p><strong>Importante:</strong> el certificado se solicita en cuanto se "
"aplica la configuración. Con la validación HTTP, el nombre de host ya debe "
"apuntar a este servidor: los intentos fallidos cuentan para el límite de "
"Let's Encrypt (5 por hora por nombre de host). Si el DNS todavía no está "
"listo, use la validación DNS.</p>\n"
"    "

#: app_gateway/views.py:306
msgid ""
"\n"
"        <div class=\"alert alert-warning\">\n"
"            This hostname is used to access WireGuard WebAdmin. If the "
"certificate cannot be issued,\n"
"            your browser will show a security warning until the problem is "
"fixed.\n"
"        </div>\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        <div class=\"alert alert-warning\">\n"
"            Este hostname se utiliza para acceder a WireGuard WebAdmin. Si "
"no se puede emitir el certificado,\n"
"            su navegador mostrará una advertencia de seguridad hasta que se "
"corrija el problema.\n"
"        </div>\n"
"        "

