"\n"
"        <h5>Cluster Enabled</h5>\n"
"        <p>When disabled, workers are refused and shut down their WireGuard "
"interfaces, and App Gateway applications are only published by this primary "
"server. Requires the WireGuard status cache.</p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Primary Enable WireGuard</h5>\n"
"        <p>Mirror mode only. When disabled, this primary server stops its "
"WireGuard interfaces once the configuration is applied, is no longer offered "
"when downloading peer configurations and VPN invites, and only publishes "
"WireGuard WebAdmin in the App Gateway. Workers keep receiving the "
"configuration, and the primary server keeps managing the certificates used "
"by them. Make sure you can reach WireGuard WebAdmin without the VPN of this "
"server before disabling it.</p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Cluster Mode</h5>\n"
"        <p><strong>Mirror</strong>: every worker receives the same WireGuard "
"instances, peers, firewall and DNS configuration. Peers can connect to any "
"server.</p>\n"
"        <p><strong>Distributed</strong>: each WireGuard instance runs only "
"on the server selected in the instance settings (the primary server by "
"default). Peers connect to that server. Firewall rules cannot be bound to a "
"specific instance interface: use wg+ or IP addresses. After changing the "
"mode, apply the WireGuard configuration so the primary server stops the "
"instances that moved to workers.</p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Worker Display</h5>\n"
"        <p>How workers are named in server selections (peer configuration "
"downloads and VPN invites).</p>\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        <h5>Cluster habilitado</h5>\n"
"        <p>Cuando está deshabilitado, los workers son rechazados y apagan "
"sus interfaces WireGuard, y las aplicaciones del App Gateway solo las "
"publica este servidor primario. Requiere la caché de estado de WireGuard.</"
"p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Habilitar WireGuard primario</h5>\n"
"        <p>Muestra este servidor primario como opción al descargar "
"configuraciones de peer e invitaciones de VPN.</p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Modo de cluster</h5>\n"
"        <p><strong>Mirror</strong>: todos los workers reciben las mismas "
"instancias de WireGuard, peers, firewall y configuración de DNS. Los peers "
"pueden conectarse a cualquier servidor.</p>\n"
"        <p><strong>Distributed</strong>: cada instancia de WireGuard se "
"ejecuta solo en el servidor seleccionado en la configuración de la instancia "
"(el servidor primario por defecto). Los peers se conectan a ese servidor. "
"Las reglas de firewall no pueden vincularse a la interfaz de una instancia "
"específica: use wg+ o direcciones IP. Después de cambiar el modo, aplique la "
"configuración de WireGuard para que el servidor primario detenga las "
"instancias que pasaron a los workers.</p>\n"
"\n"
"        <h5>Visualización del worker</h5>\n"
"        <p>Cómo se nombran los workers en las selecciones de servidor "
"(descargas de configuraciones de peer e invitaciones de VPN).</p>\n"
"        "

